{"id": "De_q18MxWF4", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Hanuman ji have 5 FACES? 🐒🦁🦅🐗🐴 Only one of them is a monkey… and the reason is a kidnapping.\n\nDuring the Lanka war, Ravana's brother AHIRAVANA, the sorcerer-king of Patala, used his magic to carry off Ram and Lakshman while they slept, to sacrifice them in the underworld.\n\nHanuman dove after them. At the gate of Patala stood a guard, half vanara, half fish, who said he was Hanuman's own son: Makardhwaja, born when a drop of Hanuman's sweat fell into the sea and a fish swallowed it. Hanuman tied him up and went in.\n\nInside, Ahiravana's life was hidden in FIVE lamps, burning in FIVE directions. Blow out all five at once, or he could never die.\n\nOne mouth. Five lamps. So Hanuman became PANCHMUKHI:\n🐒 Hanuman (east): victory\n🦁 Narasimha (south): fearlessness\n🦅 Garuda (west): protection\n🐗 Varaha (north): prosperity\n🐴 Hayagriva (the sky): knowledge\nAll five blew at once, and Ram and Lakshman were saved.\n\n(This story isn't in Valmiki. It comes from the Ahiravana legend in the regional Ramayanas, the Krittivasi and the Ananda Ramayana, and from temple tradition. The faces and their blessings are from the Panchamukha Hanumat Kavacham.)\n\n📚 Want stories like this for your little ones? Our Rishi Katha picture books: Books 1–3 as a set for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💬 Which FACE do you need today? Comment it!\n🔁 Save this for the next time you see Panchmukhi Hanuman ji, and share it with someone who didn't know.\n\n#hanuman #panchmukhihanuman #hanumanji #jaibajrangbali #bajrangbali #ramayan #ramayana #hindumythology #sanatandharma #indianmythology #storiesforkids #mythologyforkids #rishikatha #hanumanchalisa", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793097881, "like_count": 9187, "comment_count": 47, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-4503408076567898a", 